⊕meta⊕
name = "chain-invoke-leaf"
description = "Invoke-chain leaf. Logs the marker it was handed. Runnable standalone (skyway run chain-invoke-leaf --var marker=hi) or as the invoke target of chain-invoke-root."
params.marker.type = "string"
params.marker.description = "Marker string echoed to the chain-test log."
trigger.manual = true
output_style = "terse"
⊕⊕

※land※
Bash root node. Appends a land marker (with the received marker var) to the shared chain-test log.
※※

§land§
bash = "echo \"invoke-leaf:land marker=${SKY_MARKER:-none} $(date -u +%s)\" >> /tmp/skyway-chain-test.log"
§§

※※
chain-invoke-leaf: invoke target

Pure bash, zero cost. Receives marker as $SKY_MARKER and logs it. Used to prove
that an explicit invoke reaches a leaf regardless of its enabled state.
※※
